<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch company results week of April 28.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch company results week of April 28.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of Dutch company results for the week of April 28 - May 2.</p>
<p>DATE--COMPANY--PERIOD--PROFIT----------CONSENSUS---RANGE-----PVS</p>
<p>29/4 DSM	 Q1 97  net ord ops		217    185/235  215</p>
<p>1/5  RD/Shell  Q1 97  net pft current costs 1636  1480/1880 1625</p>
<p>1/5  RD/Shell  Q1 97  net pft		   1526  1330/1730 1743</p>
<p>2/5  Unilever  Q1 97  net pft current rates  923    885/958  808</p>
<p>2/5  KNP BT    Q1 97  net pft		    45     40/48     50</p>
<p>NOTES - Profit figures exclude extraordinary items and are in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated. They are stated before deduction of preference dividends where applicable.</p>
<p>* ROYAL DUTCH/SHELL estimates are in millions of sterling and refer to historic cost net profit and current cost net profit.</p>
<p>* UNILEVER estimates are in guilders and at current currency rates.</p>
<p>* KNP BT said on March 19, its first quarter results would probably be slightly lower than those of Q1 1996.</p>
<p>FORECASTS CONTRIBUTED BY: Amstgeld, Bangert Pontier, Delta Lloyd Bank, Generale Bank, Kempen &amp; Co, Labouchere, Van Lanschot, Rabo/IRIS.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
